  displayName: Horse
  category: 1
  summary: Horses are strong, plant-eating animals with hooves. For hundreds of years
    they've helped people plow fields, carry things and travel!
  facts:
  - Horses only sleep about 2 to 3 hours a day, and they often nap standing up!
  - Horses have the biggest eyes of any animal that lives on land!
  - A horse's height is measured in "hands." One hand equals 4 inches!
  sources:
  - Britannica for Students (Britannica Kids). Horse. https://kids.britannica.com/students/article/horse/274947
